# Coach speech (Hungarian): the appraisal after the game (src/coach/appraisal.cpp).
# Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang (its header documents every placeholder).
# The appraisal is always positive and never blames. The coach says "te" (tegezés) and speaks of himself
# as "én"; Hungarian has no grammatical gender, nothing agrees with the player.
#
# Names inserted by {text}, {theme}, {level}: {text} takes no form (a form would need a key in common.lang),
# so each name is written to fit every sentence that inserts it, in the nominative:
#   appraisal.phase.*   with the article ("a középjáték"): "{text} ment a legjobban", "{text} volt".
#   appraisal.reason.*  an adverbial said after "Döntetlen, {text}." ("lépésismétlés miatt").
#   theme.*             an infinitive phrase in lower case, no full stop ("figyelni a kettős támadásokra"),
#                       said after a colon, "fontos" or "próbálj meg".
#   appraisal.level.*   the level name of the coach page in „…” WITH its article, as a/az depends on the
#                       name: "{level} szintre" = "a „Kezdő” szintre", "az „Első lépések” szintre".
# {opening:def} = the opening's name with its article ("a szicíliai védelem"); bare {opening} only after a
# colon or alone.
# Move numbers: {n:ord} ("21.", spoken "huszonegyedik") never after "a"/"az": "{n:ord} lépésként",
# "a játszma {n:ord} lépésében", "{n:ord} lépés: {move}". A move stands alone, before "helyett" or "lépéssel".
# Accuracy: {acc:percent} = "85%", {acc:percent_adj} = "85%-os" (spoken "nyolcvanöt százalék(os)").
# {n:time} never starts a sentence (its "egyszer" would stay in lower case).

